# Hutton (2002)-style self-replicating chains, "Evolvable self-replicating molecules
# in an artificial chemistry", Artificial Life 8(4). Template: e8.a1.b1 ... f1
# (insert one with data/replicator.mol, key I in acsim).
#
# Syntax:  <type><state> (+|.) <type><state> -> <type><state> (+|.) <type><state> [@ prob]
#   '+'   the two atoms are NOT bonded        '.'  the two atoms are bonded
#   a..z  a concrete type
#   *     any type; in a product: keep the type of the reactant at that position
#   X..Z  a type variable: the same letter twice on the left = same type
# The first matching rule (file order) wins. Press R in acsim to reload this file.

# --- physics -------------------------------------------------------------
set temperature 0.3
set react_range 1.7
set food abcdef

# all bonds: springs of rest length 1.5 (> contact distance 2r = 1) so that a new atom can
# slip between template atoms to reach the right side; react_range 1.7 (in units of 2r)
# lets the copy strand reach it. With len=1.0 the copy often gets stuck on the wrong side.
spring * * k=20 len=1.5

# --- reactions -----------------------------------------------------------
e8 + e0 -> e4 . e3        # 1. the head grabs a free e: start of the copy
X4 . Y1 -> X2 . Y5        # 2. the "copy me" signal moves down the template
X5 + X0 -> X7 . X6        # 3. a template atom grabs a free atom of the SAME type
X3 + Y6 -> X2 . Y3        # 4. the growing copy bonds to the new atom
X7 . Y3 -> X4 . Y3        # 5. template atom done, pass the signal on
f4 . f3 -> f8 + f8        # 6. tail reached: release the copy's tail
X2 . Y8 -> X9 . Y1        # 7. unzip, moving back up both strands
*9 . *9 -> *8 + *8        # 8. break the template/copy rung (wildcard form)
